WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.226
Most business photos are landscape, but Reels, Shorts and TikTok want a tall 9:16

2
00:00:08.226 --> 00:00:08.835
frame.

3
00:00:08.835 --> 00:00:11.540
That mismatch has three solutions.

4
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.516
You can crop to fill the frame, which keeps a full-screen image but removes more

5
00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:19.191
than sixty percent of a wide photo's width.

6
00:00:19.191 --> 00:00:24.488
You can letterbox on a plain colour, which keeps the whole photo but leaves empty

7
00:00:24.488 --> 00:00:24.880
bands.

8
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.117
Or you can place the photo over a blurred, enlarged copy of itself, filling the

9
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:34.227
frame with matching colour while the original stays untouched.

10
00:00:34.227 --> 00:00:40.171
The blurred fill works for most landscape shots: rooms, vehicles, venues.

11
00:00:40.171 --> 00:00:44.432
Cropping only works when the subject sits centred and narrow.

12
00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:48.751
Render at 1080 by 1920 pixels.

13
00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:54.375
Keep captions clear of each platform's interface overlays, which sit along the

14
00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:55.961
bottom and right side.

15
00:00:55.961 --> 00:01:01.913
Make the 9:16 and 16:9 cuts from the same source to avoid editing twice.
